node_modules/
out/
dist/
samples/*
!samples/README.md
# The IfcOpenShell ground truth is generated from a real project model and carries its
# metadata (file name, storey names, GUIDs, site latitude/longitude, element property
# sets). Regenerate it locally with scripts/expected-from-ifcopenshell.py.
tests/fixtures/*.expected.json
# Parity captures are large (24 MB for Phase 2a alone) and are regenerated on demand by
# scripts/screenshot.cjs and scripts/parity-prototype.cjs. tests/parity/<phase>/README.md
# carries the commands and the measured differences, and that is what belongs in the repo.
tests/parity/**/*.png
tests/parity/**/*.jpg
# The chrome rectangles each capture writes beside its PNG (Phase 3 onwards).
tests/parity/**/*.json
.DS_Store
*.log
.env*
tmp/
# Playwright's own output from `npm run test:e2e` (scripts/safe-e2e.cjs).
test-results/
playwright-report/
# The assistant eval suite's output (scripts/ai-eval.cjs, docs/AI_EVAL.md). The cases, the
# graders and the runner are the repository's; a run's transcripts and derived report are not.
# A trace carries every tool result of a turn, which on a real model is project data.
.claude/hillclimb/**/traces/
.claude/hillclimb/**/report.html
.claude/hillclimb/**/trajectory/
# A build directory kept as an eval baseline (SGVUE_APP_OUT=out-baseline).
out-baseline/
# The AI coding assistant's own working folders: drafts, audits, worktrees and local settings.
# `.claude/hillclimb/` stays tracked — the eval suite's baselines, which `scripts/ai-eval.cjs`
# reads and extends.
.claude/wip/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
# Not redistributed, because their licence was never recorded (2026-10-05): the design tool's
# runtime and starter files (design-reference/README.md) and the eval's HTML report builder
# (docs/AI_EVAL.md). A maintainer who has them may keep them in place; they are never committed.
design-reference/design/support.js
design-reference/ask-vee/support.js
design-reference/ask-vee/animations-v3.jsx
design-reference/ask-vee/tweaks-panel.jsx
scripts/eval/report/
